From 7459cdc4766043174ce2b982f6bbe7c0911279c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:47:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: don't put an absent MDIO reset GPIO

devm_gpiod_get_optional() returns NULL when the property is absent, and
stmmac_mdio_reset() only tests IS_ERR() before calling devm_gpiod_put().
With no "snps,reset" in the device tree that puts NULL, devres_release()
finds nothing to release, and WARN_ON fires on every probe:

  WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 1 at drivers/gpio/gpiolib-devres.c:327 devm_gpiod_put+0x34/0x44
  Call trace:
   devm_gpiod_put+0x34/0x44
   stmmac_mdio_reset+0x110/0x150
   __mdiobus_register+0x228/0x298

Boards whose PHY needs no reset line hit this every boot: the RK3528 TV
boxes use an integrated FEPHY and never set the property.
stmmac_mdio_idle() already checks for NULL.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_mdio.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_mdio.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_mdio.c
index 85ccc23..30a74c7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_mdio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_mdio.c
@@ -405,7 +405,8 @@ int stmmac_mdio_reset(struct mii_bus *bus)
 			msleep(DIV_ROUND_UP(delays[2], 1000));
 
 		/* put reset gpio resource for next time */
-		devm_gpiod_put(priv->device, reset_gpio);
+		if (reset_gpio)
+			devm_gpiod_put(priv->device, reset_gpio);
 	}
 #endif
 
